From 1f7ed6caa09d50a896ad73e9021a5a99bc399354 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:14:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 44/45] Setup wizard: Library Files page on Android, and
 Preferences > Run Setup Wizard

Android: the app bundles the symbol and footprint libraries and the
templates but not the 3D models (3.2 GB).  A Library Files page, before
the library tables page, downloads the 3D models from KiCad's library
repositories on GitLab, updates the bundled libraries to the newest
release of their series (from GitLab's tag list), or installs libraries
from zip/tar/tar.gz archives.  Archives are taken apart by content
(*.kicad_symdir, *.pretty, *.3dshapes, Projects/, the stock tables, ...),
so the GitLab archives and zips of a desktop KiCad's folders both work.
Downloads unpack into a staging folder; library folders replace the
installed ones only when complete, template files are merged.  The page
is shown once at first start.

Preferences > Run Setup Wizard runs the wizard again at any time, with
the pages that can be run again (Library Files, Updates & Privacy, the
latter starting from the current settings); cancelling changes nothing.

Android: libcurl uses OpenSSL, which has no CA bundle there; the system
certificates are passed as an in-memory bundle (their file names use
OpenSSL's old hash, so they don't work as a CAPATH).

The library tables page wraps its text to the page width on Android,
where it was cut off.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
